# Top-level .dockerignore, applying to every POC's Docker build now that each POC's Dockerfile
# builds from this top-level directory as its context (needed so a Dockerfile can COPY in the
# sibling insightflow_core/ package it depends on — see insightflow_core/README.md and each
# POC's own Dockerfile comment for why). Docker only ever reads ONE .dockerignore, from the
# context root, so this replaces poc3_dashboard_generation/.dockerignore (poc2 never had one) —
# per-POC ignore files stopped being read the moment the build context moved up a level.
.venv/
__pycache__/
.git/
.env
*.md
**/tests/
*.duckdb
.pytest_cache/
backend/.uploads/

# Each POC's real-Olist example data is multi-MB and never COPY'd into an image anyway (only
# each POC's own small data/ sample is) — excluded from the build context entirely so it isn't
# even sent to the Docker daemon. data/ itself is deliberately NOT excluded here: it's the small
# sample dataset each POC's Dockerfile does COPY in and its README's example commands reference
# by relative path — a parent-directory exclusion can't be selectively un-excluded once a
# Dockerfile tries to COPY it back in (learned the hard way during POC 2's closure sweep).
poc2_analytics_engine/examples/
poc3_dashboard_generation/examples/
